---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { loadContent } from "../../lib/content";
import { calBookingUrl } from "../../lib/site";

const { provider } = loadContent();
---

<Layout
  title={`Circles | CBSE Class 10 Maths | ${provider.name}`}
  description="CBSE Class 10 Maths Chapter 10 study notes on Circles. Master tangent theorems (radius perpendicular to tangent, equal external tangents), cyclic quadrilaterals, circumscribed polygons, and an interactive 20-question board quiz."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="small" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/subjects/">Subjects</a> / <a href="/resources/">Resources</a> / Circles
    </nav>

    <div class="resource-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">CBSE Class 10 · Mathematics · Chapter 10</span>
      <h1>Circles</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Explore tangents to circles, understand Theorems 10.1 and 10.2, solve circumscribed polygon questions, and master board exam circle geometry proofs.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Core Concepts -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Key Concepts &amp; Theorems</h2>

      <div class="grid two concept-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>⭕ Tangent to a Circle</h3>
          <p class="formula">Line intersecting circle at exactly ONE point</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li><strong>Tangent:</strong> A line that touches the circle at only one point. The common point is called the <strong>point of contact</strong>.</li>
            <li><strong>Secant:</strong> A line that intersects a circle in two distinct points.</li>
            <li>A circle can have <strong>infinitely many tangents</strong>, but at any single point on the circle, there is <strong>only one tangent</strong>.</li>
            <li>A circle can have at most <strong>two parallel tangents</strong> at a time (drawn at the endpoints of a diameter).</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>📐 Theorem 10.1: Radius Perpendicular to Tangent</h3>
          <p class="formula">OP ⊥ XY at point of contact P</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li><strong>Statement:</strong> The tangent at any point of a circle is perpendicular to the radius through the point of contact.</li>
            <li><strong>Proof logic:</strong> Any point Q on the tangent line XY other than P must lie outside the circle. Therefore, <code>OQ &gt; OP</code> (radius). Since OP is the shortest distance from center O to line XY, <code>OP ⊥ XY</code>.</li>
            <li>By Pythagoras theorem in right ΔOPT: <code>OT² = OP² + PT²</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>⭐ Theorem 10.2: Lengths of External Tangents</h3>
          <p class="formula">PQ = PR (Tangents from external point P)</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li><strong>Statement:</strong> The lengths of tangents drawn from an external point to a circle are equal.</li>
            <li><strong>Proof:</strong> In right triangles ΔOPQ and ΔOPR:
              <br/>• <code>OQ = OR</code> (Radii)
              <br/>• <code>OP = OP</code> (Common hypotenuse)
              <br/>• <code>∠OQP = ∠ORP = 90°</code> (Theorem 10.1)
              <br/>⟹ <code>ΔOPQ ≅ ΔOPR</code> (by RHS congruence).
              <br/>Therefore, <code>PQ = PR</code> (CPCT).
            </li>
            <li><strong>Angle bisector:</strong> Line OP bisects the angle between the two tangents (<code>∠OPQ = ∠OPR</code>) and angle subtended at center (<code>∠POQ = ∠POR</code>).</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>🔷 Circumscribing Quadrilaterals &amp; Parallelograms</h3>
          <p class="formula">AB + CD = AD + BC</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>If a quadrilateral <em>ABCD</em> circumscribes a circle, then:
              <br/><code>AB + CD = AD + BC</code> (Sum of opposite sides are equal).
            </li>
            <li>A parallelogram circumscribing a circle is always a <strong>rhombus</strong> (and if it has a right angle, a <strong>square</strong>).</li>
            <li>The angle between the two tangents drawn from an external point to a circle is <strong>supplementary</strong> to the angle subtended by the line segment joining the points of contact at the center: <code>∠PTQ + ∠POQ = 180°</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Visual Diagrams Section -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Visual Concepts: External Tangent Kite &amp; Circumscribed Quadrilateral</h2>

      <div class="grid two">
        <div class="card visual-card">
          <div class="visual-badge">Visual Diagram 1 · External Tangents &amp; Kite Structure</div>
          <div class="svg-container">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 460 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Tangents from an external point">
              <rect width="460" height="250" fill="#f8fafc" rx="8"/>
              
              <!-- Circle with Center O(280, 125) radius 65 -->
              <circle cx="280" cy="125" r="65" fill="#f1f5f9" stroke="#0f766e" stroke-width="2.5"/>
              <circle cx="280" cy="125" r="4" fill="#0f766e"/>
              <text x="295" y="130" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0f766e">O</text>

              <!-- External Point P(60, 125) -->
              <circle cx="60" cy="125" r="5" fill="#ef4444"/>
              <text x="45" y="130" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626">P</text>

              <!-- Tangent Points Q(235, 78) and R(235, 172) -->
              <!-- Tangent PQ -->
              <line x1="60" y1="125" x2="235" y2="78" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2.5"/>
              <!-- Tangent PR -->
              <line x1="60" y1="125" x2="235" y2="172" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2.5"/>

              <!-- Radii OQ and OR -->
              <line x1="280" y1="125" x2="235" y2="78" stroke="#0f766e" stroke-width="2"/>
              <line x1="280" y1="125" x2="235" y2="172" stroke="#0f766e" stroke-width="2"/>

              <!-- Center line OP -->
              <line x1="60" y1="125" x2="280" y2="125" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4"/>

              <!-- Tangent points dots -->
              <circle cx="235" cy="78" r="4" fill="#0284c7"/>
              <text x="230" y="68" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">Q</text>
              <circle cx="235" cy="172" r="4" fill="#0284c7"/>
              <text x="230" y="190" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">R</text>

              <!-- 90 deg symbols at Q and R -->
              <rect x="235" y="78" width="10" height="10" transform="rotate(-30 235 78)" fill="none" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              <rect x="235" y="162" width="10" height="10" transform="rotate(30 235 162)" fill="none" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="1.5"/>

              <!-- Labels -->
              <text x="140" y="90" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">PQ</text>
              <text x="140" y="165" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">PR</text>
              <text x="260" y="98" font-size="10" fill="#0f766e">r</text>
              <text x="260" y="155" font-size="10" fill="#0f766e">r</text>

              <!-- Equality Banner -->
              <rect x="150" y="215" width="160" height="24" rx="4" fill="#0f766e"/>
              <text x="230" y="231" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">PQ = PR &nbsp;(Theorem 10.2)</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="visual-caption">External point tangents are equal (PQ = PR); ΔOPQ ≅ ΔOPR; ∠QPR + ∠QOR = 180°.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card visual-card">
          <div class="visual-badge">Visual Diagram 2 · Circumscribing Quadrilateral Sum Property</div>
          <div class="svg-container">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 460 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Circumscribing quadrilateral property">
              <rect width="460" height="250" fill="#f8fafc" rx="8"/>
              
              <!-- Inscribed Circle -->
              <circle cx="230" cy="125" r="60" fill="#f1f5f9" stroke="#0f766e" stroke-width="2"/>
              <circle cx="230" cy="125" r="3" fill="#0f766e"/>

              <!-- Quadrilateral ABCD -->
              <polygon points="120,40 340,40 370,210 90,210" fill="none" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="2.5"/>
              <text x="110" y="35" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">A</text>
              <text x="350" y="35" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">B</text>
              <text x="380" y="220" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">C</text>
              <text x="75" y="220" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#0284c7">D</text>

              <!-- Points of Contact P, Q, R, S -->
              <circle cx="230" cy="65" r="4" fill="#ef4444"/>
              <text x="230" y="58" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626" text-anchor="middle">P</text>

              <circle cx="290" cy="125" r="4" fill="#ef4444"/>
              <text x="305" y="129" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626">Q</text>

              <circle cx="230" cy="185" r="4" fill="#ef4444"/>
              <text x="230" y="200" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626" text-anchor="middle">R</text>

              <circle cx="170" cy="125" r="4" fill="#ef4444"/>
              <text x="155" y="129" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#dc2626">S</text>

              <!-- Formula Banner -->
              <rect x="110" y="218" width="240" height="24" rx="4" fill="#0284c7"/>
              <text x="230" y="234" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">AB + CD = AD + BC</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="visual-caption">Since AP = AS, BP = BQ, CR = CQ, DR = DS, adding gives AB + CD = AD + BC.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Solved Step-by-Step Problem -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Exemplar Board Problem: Quadrilateral Circumscribing a Circle</h2>
      <div class="card" style="padding:1.75rem; background:var(--paper)">
        <h3 style="color:var(--brand);margin-top:0">Problem: A quadrilateral ABCD is drawn to circumscribe a circle. Prove that AB + CD = AD + BC. Hence prove that a parallelogram circumscribing a circle is a rhombus.</h3>
        <div style="font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.7; color:var(--text)">
          <p><strong>Part 1 (Prove AB + CD = AD + BC):</strong>
            <br/>Let the circle touch sides <em>AB, BC, CD, DA</em> at points <em>P, Q, R, S</em> respectively.
            <br/>By Theorem 10.2, the tangents drawn from an external point to a circle are equal in length:
            <br/>• From vertex A: <code>AP = AS &nbsp;...(1)</code>
            <br/>• From vertex B: <code>BP = BQ &nbsp;...(2)</code>
            <br/>• From vertex C: <code>CR = CQ &nbsp;...(3)</code>
            <br/>• From vertex D: <code>DR = DS &nbsp;...(4)</code>
          </p>
          <p>Adding equations (1), (2), (3), and (4):
            <br/><code>(AP + BP) + (CR + DR) = (AS + DS) + (BQ + CQ)</code>
            <br/><code>AB + CD = AD + BC</code>. [Hence Proved]
          </p>
          <p><strong>Part 2 (Deduction for Parallelogram to Rhombus):</strong>
            <br/>If <em>ABCD</em> is a parallelogram, then opposite sides are equal:
            <br/><code>AB = CD</code> and <code>AD = BC</code>.
            <br/>Substituting into <code>AB + CD = AD + BC</code>:
            <br/><code>AB + AB = AD + AD &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; 2AB = 2AD &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; AB = AD</code>.
            <br/>Since adjacent sides of parallelogram ABCD are equal (<code>AB = AD</code>), all four sides are equal: <code>AB = BC = CD = DA</code>.
            <br/><strong>Conclusion:</strong> A parallelogram circumscribing a circle is a <strong>rhombus</strong>. [Hence Proved]
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Interactive 20-Question Quiz -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Interactive CBSE Board Exam Quiz (20 Questions)</h2>
      <p class="muted">Test your concepts on tangent theorems, right-triangle radius calculations, external tangents, and circumscribed polygons.</p>

      <div class="quiz-container card" id="quiz-box">
        <div class="quiz-header-bar">
          <span class="quiz-counter" id="quiz-counter">Question 1 of 20</span>
          <span class="quiz-score" id="quiz-score">Score: 0 / 20</span>
        </div>

        <div class="quiz-question-body">
          <p class="quiz-q-text" id="quiz-question">Loading question...</p>
          <div class="quiz-options-list" id="quiz-options"></div>
          <div class="quiz-feedback" id="quiz-feedback"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="quiz-footer-actions">
          <button class="button secondary" id="quiz-prev-btn" disabled>← Previous</button>
          <button class="button" id="quiz-next-btn" disabled>Next Question →</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="quiz-completed-banner card" id="quiz-result-box" style="display:none; text-align:center; padding:2.5rem;">
        <h3>Quiz Completed! 🎉</h3>
        <p class="quiz-final-score" id="quiz-final-score" style="font-size:1.4rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--brand); margin:1rem 0;"></p>
        <p id="quiz-final-msg" class="muted"></p>
        <button class="button" id="quiz-restart-btn" style="margin-top:1rem;">Retake Quiz</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="cta-banner">
      <h2>Need personalized Maths guidance for Class 10?</h2>
      <p>Book a free {provider.trial.duration_minutes}-minute trial session with {provider.tutor_name} (online or at-home) to master circle theorems, geometric proofs, and board exam presentation.</p>
      <a class="button" href={calBookingUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book Free Trial</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
(function() {
  const quizData = [
    {
      q: "From a point Q, the length of the tangent to a circle is 24 cm and the distance of Q from the center is 25 cm. The radius of the circle is:",
      options: ["7 cm", "12 cm", "15 cm", "24.5 cm"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Radius r = √(OQ² - QT²) = √(25² - 24²) = √(625 - 576) = √49 = 7 cm."
    },
    {
      q: "If tangents PA and PB from a point P to a circle with center O are inclined to each other at an angle of 80°, then ∠POA is equal to:",
      options: ["50°", "60°", "70°", "80°"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "In quadrilateral OAPB: ∠AOB = 180° - 80° = 100°. Line OP bisects ∠AOB: ∠POA = 100° / 2 = 50°."
    },
    {
      q: "The maximum number of parallel tangents that a circle can have at a time is:",
      options: ["1", "2", "4", "Infinitely many"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Parallel tangents can only be drawn at the opposite endpoints of a diameter. Hence, a circle can have at most 2 parallel tangents."
    },
    {
      q: "If TP and TQ are the two tangents to a circle with center O so that ∠POQ = 110°, then ∠PTQ is equal to:",
      options: ["60°", "70°", "80°", "90°"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "In quadrilateral OPTQ: ∠OPT = ∠OQT = 90°. Since sum of angles is 360°, ∠PTQ + ∠POQ = 180° ⟹ ∠PTQ = 180° - 110° = 70°."
    },
    {
      q: "A line intersecting a circle in two distinct points is called a:",
      options: ["Tangent", "Secant", "Diameter", "Chord"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "A line intersecting a circle in two distinct points is called a secant (whereas a tangent touches in only one point)."
    },
    {
      q: "If a parallelogram circumscribes a circle, it must be a:",
      options: ["Rectangle", "Square", "Rhombus", "Trapezium"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "For a circumscribed quadrilateral, AB + CD = AD + BC. In a parallelogram, AB = CD and AD = BC, which implies 2AB = 2AD ⟹ AB = AD. A parallelogram with adjacent sides equal is a rhombus."
    },
    {
      q: "The length of the tangent drawn from a point 8 cm away from the center of a circle of radius 6 cm is:",
      options: ["√7 cm", "2√7 cm", "10 cm", "5 cm"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Length = √(d² - r²) = √(8² - 6²) = √(64 - 36) = √28 = 2√7 cm."
    },
    {
      q: "In two concentric circles of radii 5 cm and 3 cm, the length of the chord of the larger circle which touches the smaller circle is:",
      options: ["4 cm", "6 cm", "8 cm", "10 cm"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "The radius of the inner circle is perpendicular to the chord and bisects it. Half-chord = √(5² - 3²) = √(25 - 9) = 4 cm. Full chord = 2 × 4 = 8 cm."
    },
    {
      q: "If quadrilateral ABCD is drawn to circumscribe a circle and AB = 6 cm, BC = 7 cm, CD = 4 cm, then AD is:",
      options: ["3 cm", "4 cm", "5 cm", "6 cm"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "AB + CD = AD + BC ⟹ 6 + 4 = AD + 7 ⟹ 10 = AD + 7 ⟹ AD = 3 cm."
    },
    {
      q: "At one end A of a diameter AB of a circle of radius 5 cm, tangent XAY is drawn to the circle. The length of the chord CD parallel to XY and at a distance 8 cm from A is:",
      options: ["4 cm", "5 cm", "6 cm", "8 cm"],
      answer: 3,
      explanation: "Distance from center O to chord CD = 8 - 5 = 3 cm. Half-chord length = √(r² - d²) = √(5² - 3²) = 4 cm. Full chord CD = 2 × 4 = 8 cm."
    },
    {
      q: "How many tangents can be drawn to a circle from a point inside the circle?",
      options: ["0", "1", "2", "Infinite"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Any line through a point inside the circle intersects the circle in two points (a secant). No tangent can be drawn from an interior point."
    },
    {
      q: "If an angle between two tangents drawn from a point P to a circle of radius 'a' and center O is 90°, then OP equals:",
      options: ["a", "a√2", "2a", "a/√2"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "In quadrilateral OAPB, ∠A = ∠B = 90° and ∠P = 90° ⟹ ∠O = 90°. OAPB is a square of side a. Diagonals of square of side a are a√2. Hence OP = a√2."
    },
    {
      q: "Two concentric circles have radii 13 cm and 5 cm. A chord of the larger circle is tangent to the smaller circle. Its length is:",
      options: ["12 cm", "18 cm", "24 cm", "26 cm"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "Half-length = √(13² - 5²) = √(169 - 25) = √144 = 12 cm. Full length = 2 × 12 = 24 cm."
    },
    {
      q: "If PA and PB are tangents to a circle with center O such that ∠APB = 50°, then ∠OAB is equal to:",
      options: ["25°", "50°", "40°", "75°"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "PA = PB ⟹ ΔPAB is isosceles. In ΔPAB: ∠PAB = ∠PBA = (180° - 50°)/2 = 65°. Since radius OA ⊥ PA: ∠OAP = 90°. Therefore, ∠OAB = 90° - 65° = 25°."
    },
    {
      q: "In a triangle ABC circumscribing a circle, if AB = 12 cm, BC = 8 cm, and AC = 10 cm, then length of AD (where D is point of contact on AB) is:",
      options: ["7 cm", "5 cm", "3 cm", "6 cm"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Semi-perimeter s = (12 + 8 + 10)/2 = 15 cm. AD = s - BC = 15 - 8 = 7 cm."
    },
    {
      q: "The angle between two tangents drawn from an external point to a circle and the angle subtended by the line segment joining the points of contact at the center are:",
      options: ["Complementary", "Supplementary", "Equal", "Vertically opposite"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Since the radii are perpendicular to tangents (90° each), the remaining two opposite angles in the quadrilateral sum to 180° (supplementary)."
    },
    {
      q: "If a chord AB subtends an angle of 60° at the center of a circle, then the angle between the tangents at A and B is:",
      options: ["60°", "120°", "90°", "30°"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Angle between tangents = 180° - (angle subtended at center) = 180° - 60° = 120°."
    },
    {
      q: "Tangents drawn at the ends of a diameter of a circle are always:",
      options: ["Perpendicular", "Parallel", "Intersecting at 45°", "None of these"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Both tangents are perpendicular to the same diameter (90° + 90° = 180° consecutive interior angles). Hence, they are parallel."
    },
    {
      q: "A circle touches all the four sides of a quadrilateral ABCD whose sides are AB = 6 cm, BC = 9 cm, and CD = 8 cm. The length of side AD is:",
      options: ["5 cm", "6 cm", "7 cm", "8 cm"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "AB + CD = AD + BC ⟹ 6 + 8 = AD + 9 ⟹ 14 = AD + 9 ⟹ AD = 5 cm."
    },
    {
      q: "In right triangle ABC right-angled at B, BC = 12 cm and AB = 5 cm. The radius of the circle inscribed in the triangle is:",
      options: ["1 cm", "2 cm", "3 cm", "4 cm"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Hypotenuse AC = √(5² + 12²) = 13 cm. Inradius r = (AB + BC - AC) / 2 = (5 + 12 - 13) / 2 = 4 / 2 = 2 cm."
    }
  ];

  let currentIdx = 0;
  let userAnswers = new Array(quizData.length).fill(null);

  const qText = document.getElementById("quiz-question");
  const optionsBox = document.getElementById("quiz-options");
  const feedbackBox = document.getElementById("quiz-feedback");
  const counterBox = document.getElementById("quiz-counter");
  const scoreBox = document.getElementById("quiz-score");
  const prevBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-prev-btn");
  const nextBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-next-btn");
  const quizBox = document.getElementById("quiz-box");
  const resultBox = document.getElementById("quiz-result-box");
  const finalScore = document.getElementById("quiz-final-score");
  const finalMsg = document.getElementById("quiz-final-msg");
  const restartBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-restart-btn");

  function renderQuestion(idx) {
    const item = quizData[idx];
    counterBox.textContent = `Question ${idx + 1} of ${quizData.length}`;
    qText.textContent = item.q;
    optionsBox.innerHTML = "";
    feedbackBox.textContent = "";
    feedbackBox.className = "quiz-feedback";

    const selected = userAnswers[idx];

    item.options.forEach((optText, oIdx) => {
      const btn = document.createElement("button");
      btn.className = "quiz-opt-btn";
      btn.textContent = `${String.fromCharCode(65 + oIdx)}. ${optText}`;

      if (selected !== null) {
        btn.disabled = true;
        if (oIdx === item.answer) {
          btn.classList.add("opt-correct");
        } else if (oIdx === selected) {
          btn.classList.add("opt-wrong");
        }
      } else {
        btn.onclick = () => selectOption(oIdx);
      }

      optionsBox.appendChild(btn);
    });

    if (selected !== null) {
      if (selected === item.answer) {
        feedbackBox.textContent = `✓ Correct! ${item.explanation}`;
        feedbackBox.classList.add("feedback-correct");
      } else {
        feedbackBox.textContent = `✗ Incorrect. Correct answer is option ${String.fromCharCode(65 + item.answer)}. ${item.explanation}`;
        feedbackBox.classList.add("feedback-wrong");
      }
    }

    prevBtn.disabled = idx === 0;
    nextBtn.disabled = selected === null;
    nextBtn.textContent = idx === quizData.length - 1 ? "Finish Quiz →" : "Next Question →";
    updateScoreDisplay();
  }

  function selectOption(oIdx) {
    userAnswers[currentIdx] = oIdx;
    renderQuestion(currentIdx);
  }

  function updateScoreDisplay() {
    let score = 0;
    userAnswers.forEach((ans, i) => {
      if (ans === quizData[i].answer) score++;
    });
    scoreBox.textContent = `Score: ${score} / ${quizData.length}`;
  }

  prevBtn.onclick = () => {
    if (currentIdx > 0) {
      currentIdx--;
      renderQuestion(currentIdx);
    }
  };

  nextBtn.onclick = () => {
    if (currentIdx < quizData.length - 1) {
      currentIdx++;
      renderQuestion(currentIdx);
    } else {
      finishQuiz();
    }
  };

  function finishQuiz() {
    quizBox.style.display = "none";
    resultBox.style.display = "block";
    let score = 0;
    userAnswers.forEach((ans, i) => {
      if (ans === quizData[i].answer) score++;
    });
    finalScore.textContent = `Your Final Score: ${score} / ${quizData.length} (${Math.round((score / quizData.length) * 100)}%)`;
    if (score >= 18) {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Outstanding mastery! You have exceptional command over Circle theorems, tangents, and circumscribed polygons.";
    } else if (score >= 14) {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Great job! Review concentric circles and inradius formulas to reach 100%.";
    } else {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Review the two fundamental circle theorems and exemplar proofs above, then try again!";
    }
  }

  restartBtn.onclick = () => {
    userAnswers = new Array(quizData.length).fill(null);
    currentIdx = 0;
    resultBox.style.display = "none";
    quizBox.style.display = "block";
    renderQuestion(0);
  };

  renderQuestion(0);
})();
</script>

